<title>HUNGARY: Germany '97 GDP, budget target realistic-Rexrodt.</title>
<headline>Germany '97 GDP, budget target realistic-Rexrodt.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Economic Minister Gunter Rexrodt said on Tuesday that Germany's 1997 budget and gross domestic product (GDP) growth targets are realistic.</p>
<p>&quot;I regard the 2.5 percent (GDP growth target) a realistic figure,&quot; he told a news conference in Budapest.</p>
<p>&quot;The 2.9 percent (of the GDP) budget deficit target is a realistic figure, too&quot;.</p>
</text>
